-- title:
--   Fixed fields of μ_{q+1}-subgroups on the Drinfeld curve are curves over k
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an algebra structure over the field $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$ with $q^2$ elements, and assume that the coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\ q\ k$, defined as the quotient of the polynomial ring $k[X_0,X_1]$ in two variables by the ideal generated by $\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}\ q\ k - 1$, is a domain. Let $C$ be a subgroup of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$. Inside the group of $k$-algebra automorphisms of the function field $\mathrm{drinfeldFunctionField}\ q\ k$, the fraction field of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\ q\ k$, consider the subgroup generated by the image of $C$ under the map sending $\zeta$ to `hFunctionFieldAction q k` evaluated at the element of `hSubgroup q` given by the pair consisting of the identity matrix and the unit $\zeta$ of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$. The assertion is that the fixed field $E_C$ of this subgroup satisfies [`AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver k`](def/AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver.html#L15): every nonzero element of $E_C$ has a degree-zero divisor recording its order at each place of $E_C$ over $k$, every such place has residue field finite-dimensional over $k$, and the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega[E_C/k]$ is free of rank one over $E_C$.
--
--   This records that the quotient of the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) curve by a subgroup $C$ of $\mu_{q+1}$ is again a one-variable function field over $k$, so that places, divisors, the Jacobian and Tate modules of $E_C$ may be spoken of. It is used by the full-level modular curve statements comparing subalgebras of the Drinfeld ring with formal smoothness and cardinality conditions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_isCurveOver_fixedField_hFunctionFieldAction.lean

import Mathlib
